From fa70803ff961b09f1e5d176760241f2ed6a4956a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:12:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Bugfix: save and restore the local part loads of
 distributed separators [report R. Perry]

`VdgraphStore` did not record the local part loads, so that restoring
a saved separator with `vdgraphStoreUpdt()` left `complocload[]` with
the values of the separator computed since. After a selection ('|')
strategy, `vdgraphSeparateBd()` passed the stale local loads to
`dgraphBand()` as anchor loads, and `vdgraphSeparateZr()`, which
rightly trusts the global part sizes to skip `vdgraphZero()`, kept
them as well.

Save and restore the local loads of both parts, deriving the local
separator load as is done for the global loads, and make
`vdgraphCheck()` compare the local part loads, which it only summed
into global values before. Also fix the routine name in two of its
error messages.

Refs: DMO-12, PS-DMO-1
---
 src/libscotch/vdgraph.h       | 19 ++++++++++---------
 src/libscotch/vdgraph_check.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 src/libscotch/vdgraph_store.c |  9 +++++++--
 3 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

